%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% Compatibility aliases intentionally omitted from the canonical sample
%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% damage IPFS migration aliases:
%%   ipfs_managed, ipfs_kubo_api_port, ipfs_kubo_gateway_port,
%%   ipfs_kubo_swarm_port, ipfs_kubo_binary, ipfs_api, ipfs_peers,
%%   ipfs_peer_retry_interval. Put these values under damage.ipfs_runtime.
%%
%% damage.data_dir no longer controls run/report storage. Use state_dir,
%% runtime_data_dir and runs_dir.
%%
%% ECAI inference-pool aliases:
%%   code_ollama_nodes, code_ollama_health_interval_ms,
%%   code_ollama_health_timeout_ms, code_ollama_failure_threshold,
%%   code_ollama_cluster_attempts, code_ollama_queue_timeout_ms.
%% Use provider-neutral code_model_* keys instead.
%%
%% Nsecbunker compatibility aliases intentionally not shown:
%%   bunker_pubkey, bdd_contract_sha, aws_secret_bootstrap, rate_limit_backend,
%%   limits.created_at_window_seconds, limits.rate_limit_per_minute,
%%   limits.rate_limit_window_seconds.
%% The old phase4a_dev_key_script fragment entry is not consumed by runtime
%% code; Phase 4A operations use phase4a_dev_vault_path/report_dir directly.
%%
%% The old build_release_ipfs_api fragment key is not consumed by current
%% runtime code. build_release_ipfs_gateway remains the canonical public fetch
%% configuration and local validating Kubo access is configured by ipfs_runtime.
%%
%% The old top-level `sync` application configuration is removed. Use
%% damage.code_reload; DamageBDD now uses fs for development reloads.
